    "title": "2026 Houston rodeo performers: What to know about Cody Johnson",
    "text": "Cody Johnson isn't just closing out the 2026 RodeoHouston season. He's doing it with a full-length concert. That's quite a climb from his Rodeo beginnings. Johnson made his RodeoHouston debut as a last-minute replacement in 2017 for Old Dominion. He's since taken the rotating stage multiple times and solidified his place among the genre's biggest stars. In 2019, Johnson's song \"Welcome to the Show\" was used as RodeoHouston's official theme song. He was named male vocalist of the year at the 2025 Country Music Association Awards. Johnson will be joined by openers Jon Pardi and Randy Houser. The only other artist to play a full concert at RodeoHouston is George Strait, who last did it in 2022. That's quite the exclusive club.  When is Cody Johnson performing at the Houston 2026 rodeo? March 22 Previous RodeoHouston performances? 2017-19, 2022, 2023 Where is Cody Johnson from? Sebastopol What's a Cody Johnson song I might know? \"'Til You Can't\" What did Cody Johnson do before he was famous? He worked as a prison guard and a semi-pro bull rider.",
